WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:04.670
It was about 10 years into my teaching career
that I was thinking critically about: What

00:00:04.670 --> 00:00:07.720
is it that my students are doing and were
they in fact doing science?

00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:08.980
And the reality is that they weren’t.

00:00:08.980 --> 00:00:14.540
They were doing canned labs where they were
generating data that was predictable and they

00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:18.910
weren’t really having that opportunity to
fail at anything and then have to do any error

00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:20.400
analysis whatsoever.

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:22.269
And that’s just not how science works.

00:00:22.269 --> 00:00:27.869
So over the past decade in particular I worked
with other teachers here and we started to

00:00:27.869 --> 00:00:30.999
look out for broader scientific opportunities.

00:00:30.999 --> 00:00:34.330
And one of those opportunities we brought
in was this Wolbachia project which involves

00:00:34.330 --> 00:00:38.150
a lot of technical skill and a lot of pieces
and a lot of prep work.

00:00:38.150 --> 00:00:42.180
It’s five days of lab and at the end of
that five days of lab it’s not guaranteed

00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:43.180
that you’re going to get data.

00:00:43.180 --> 00:00:46.750
It’s the antithesis of the labs that we
did before, which we made sure we could fit

00:00:46.750 --> 00:00:49.640
in a 47-minute period and we’d get known
results at the end.

00:00:49.640 --> 00:00:50.590
This is the exact opposite.

